		"nodes": {
			"0": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "BOOL IN\n\nThe Bool In node is used to create a toggle switch in the patch interface.\nBecause the Bool In is an input node, it will show up in the Dashboard panel.\n\nA boolean value is either true or false; either 0 or 1.\nBooleans can be useful to toggle things on or off.\nFor example: bypass an effect.\n\nThe Bool In node can operate as a toggle or as a piano button (temporary on).\n\nMost of the time you will want to use this node for booleans. \nBut there is also the Bool node, which simply converts floats and integers to bools."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 275.28106689453125,
					"width": 924.393310546875,
					"x": 397.236083984375,
