					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 3: BOOL TO TEXTURE\n\nIn this example we are converting a Bool to a texture.\nThis will result in either a transparent(false) or white(true) pixel.\nBy setting Texture from Data node to an absolute resolution we can scale it up to patch size.\nThe To Texture node will create a Texture 2D Channel type, which is used for the RGBA channels of the Texture 2DRGBA type creature by the Texture node.\n\nTry making a Bool In for each channel and play with the color combinations you can create.\nThis is a great exercise to get into creating textures with numbers."
					}
				},
